				<r3d:description language="eng">!!!&lt;&lt;&lt; KiGGS was closed in 2024; data can still be requested &gt;&gt;&gt;!!! KiGGS is a long-term study conducted by the Robert Koch Institute (RKI) on the health of children and adolescents in Germany. The study repeatedly supplies data, representative of the country as a whole, on the health of under 18-year-olds. In addition, the children and adolescents of the first KiGGS study are repeatedly invited, and they continue to be monitored right into their adulthood.</r3d:description>
